## ⚡ Command Quick-Reference

**Commonly confused — use the featureht command:**

| Want to... | Correct command | Common mistake |
|------------|----------------|----------------|
| Close/complete a ticket | `bd close <id>` | ~~bd complete~~ (not a command), ~~bd update --status done~~ (invalid status) |
| Claim work | `bd update <id> --claim` | ~~bd update --status=in_progress~~ (works but --claim is atomic) |
| Message another agent | `{{ cmd }} nudge <target> "msg"` | ~~tmux send-keys~~ (unreliable) |
| Dispatch work to agent | `{{ cmd }} sling <ticket> <feature>` | ~~gt sling <ticket>~~ (no target = self-sling) |
| Stop my session | `{{ cmd }} engineers stop {{ .Polecat }}` | ~~gt feature stop~~ (stops feature agents, not engineers) |
| Pause feature (daemon won't restart) | `{{ cmd }} feature park <feature>` | ~~gt feature stop~~ (daemon will restart it) |
| Permanently disable feature | `{{ cmd }} feature dock <feature>` | ~~gt feature park~~ (temporary only) |

**Tickets valid statuses:** `open`, `in_progress`, `blocked`, `deferred`, `closed`, `pinned`, `hooked`
(there is NO `done` or `complete` status)

**Feature lifecycle commands (park vs dock vs stop):**
- `park/unpark` — Temporary pause. Daemon skips parked features.
- `dock/undock` — Persistent disable. Survives daemon restarts.
- `stop/start` — Immediate stop/start of feature patrol agents (QA engineer + release engineer).
- `restart/reboot` — Stop then start feature agents.

